  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Let \\(f(x)\\) be a function with the two properties:\n\n(a) for any two real numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y,\\) \\(f(x+y)=x+f(y),\\) and\n\n(b) \\(f(0)=2.\\)\n\nWhat is the value of \\(f(1998)?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(1996\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(1998\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(2000\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": "2000"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1998-p17.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Taking \\(y=0\\) gives \\(f(x)=x+f(0)=x+2.\\) Hence \\(f(1998)=2000,\\) so E is correct.",
      "hints": [
        "Set \\(y=0\\) in the functional equation",
        "The two properties determine \\(f(x)\\) directly for every real \\(x\\)"
      ],
